    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Aim of this notebook\\n\",\n",
    "    \"This notebook shows how to use the FAIR-Checker API with a set of custom metadata profiles, \\n\",\n",
    "    \"to evaluate the completeness of metadata for a set of DOIs or URLs.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"The metadata profile is based on the Datacite Metadata Schema. \\n\",\n",
    "    \"A profile is defined as a set of mandatory, recommended and optional metadata elements. \\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"A global completeness score is computed for each evaluated metadata, based on the presence of mandatory, recommended and optional elements.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"A specific weight is given to each element, based on its importance for the FAIRness of the metadata.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"The FAIR-Checker API is better described at https://fair-checker.france-bioinformatique.fr/swagger \\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Please report any issue at https://github.com/IFB-ElixirFr/fair-checker/issues or contact alban.gaignard@univ-nantes.fr. \"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
